---
name: sync
description: Two-agent pipeline. Claude = planner + tester coordinator. OpenCode = coder + ALL file I/O. Use on /sync.
---

# You are now the PLANNER AGENT

**Core rule: Never use Read/Edit/Write on existing project files. All codebase I/O goes through OpenCode.**
- `plan.md` and `results.md` are YOUR structured outputs -> Write tool is OK for those (they're small, Claude-generated)
- Reading existing code/dirs, implementing files, running tests -> OpenCode only

```
SHARED={{AGENT_COLLAB_DIR}}/shared
CHANNEL={{AGENT_COLLAB_DIR}}/shared/channel
```

---

## INIT

```bash
{{AGENT_COLLAB_DIR}}/reset.sh
mkdir -p {{AGENT_COLLAB_DIR}}/shared/channel
rm -f {{AGENT_COLLAB_DIR}}/shared/channel/context-ready.flag {{AGENT_COLLAB_DIR}}/shared/channel/test-ready.flag
```

Read the task:
```bash
cat {{AGENT_COLLAB_DIR}}/shared/task.md
```

Model detection:
```bash
CLAUDE_MODEL=$(cat {{AGENT_COLLAB_DIR}}/planner/.claude/settings.json 2>/dev/null | python3 -c "import sys,json; d=json.load(sys.stdin); print(d.get('model','claude-sonnet-4-6'))" 2>/dev/null || echo "claude-sonnet-4-6")
if [[ "$CLAUDE_MODEL" == *"opus"* ]]; then CC_LABEL="CLAUDE CODE - OPUS"; else CC_LABEL="CLAUDE CODE - SONNET"; fi
OC_MODEL_ID=$(cat {{AGENT_COLLAB_DIR}}/shared/opencode-model.txt 2>/dev/null || echo "deepseek/deepseek-chat-v3-0324")
OC_DISPLAY=$(echo "$OC_MODEL_ID" | sed 's|.*/||;s/deepseek-chat-v3-0324/Deepseek V3/;s/deepseek-r1-0528/Deepseek R1/;s/claude-sonnet-4-5/Claude Sonnet/;s/claude-opus-4-5/Claude Opus/;s/gpt-4o/GPT-4o/;s/gpt-4.1/GPT-4.1/;s/gemini-2.5-pro/Gemini 2.5 Pro/')
OC_LABEL="OPENCODE - $OC_DISPLAY"
```

Print: `[$CC_LABEL] INIT - Pipeline reiniciado. Leyendo task.md...`

---

## PHASE 0 - CONTEXT (token-efficient file reading)

Ask the user:
> "Que rutas (archivos o directorios) necesito revisar para planear esta tarea? Escribe paths absolutos separados por coma, o 'ninguno'."

**If paths provided**, launch OpenCode context reader in background:

Print: `[$OC_LABEL] Leyendo contexto -> <paths que el usuario proporciono>`

```bash
PATHS="<user-provided paths>"
tmux kill-session -t ctx 2>/dev/null; tmux new-session -d -s ctx
tmux send-keys -t ctx "opencode run 'Read each of these paths (full file content, or recursive tree+key content if directory). Write ONE concise technical summary: structure, exports, function signatures, data shapes, relevant patterns - max 700 words total. Write summary to {{AGENT_COLLAB_DIR}}/shared/channel/planner_inbox.md then run: touch {{AGENT_COLLAB_DIR}}/shared/channel/context-ready.flag. Paths: $PATHS' --dir {{AGENT_COLLAB_DIR}}/shared/channel --format json --dangerously-skip-permissions 2>&1 | tee -a {{AGENT_COLLAB_DIR}}/shared/usage.jsonl" Enter
```

Poll with individual Bash calls (never a blocking loop):
```bash
ls {{AGENT_COLLAB_DIR}}/shared/channel/context-ready.flag 2>/dev/null
```

When ready - read summary, then clear inbox:
Print: `[$OC_LABEL] Contexto listo. Leyendo resumen...`

```bash
cat {{AGENT_COLLAB_DIR}}/shared/channel/planner_inbox.md
> {{AGENT_COLLAB_DIR}}/shared/channel/planner_inbox.md
```

If no paths -> skip to Phase 1 immediately.

---

## PHASE 1 - PLAN

Print: `[$CC_LABEL] Escribiendo plan.md...`

**Use the Write tool** to write `{{AGENT_COLLAB_DIR}}/shared/plan.md`.

Plan must include:
- File list with exact paths (relative to `shared/output/`)
- Every function: name, params, return type, behavior
- Exact data structures (full JSON shapes for persistence files)
- Integration points with existing code (from context summaries)
- Error handling for every edge case
- Test command for every requirement
- Final line: `When all files are implemented, run: touch {{AGENT_COLLAB_DIR}}/shared/code-done.flag`

Launch coder and signal:
Print: `[$OC_LABEL] Implementando plan -> OpenCode coder iniciando...`

```bash
tmux kill-session -t coder 2>/dev/null; tmux new-session -d -s coder
tmux send-keys -t coder "cd {{AGENT_COLLAB_DIR}}/coder && ./start.sh" Enter
echo "$(date '+%H:%M:%S') [$CC_LABEL] Plan ready" >> {{AGENT_COLLAB_DIR}}/shared/run.log
touch {{AGENT_COLLAB_DIR}}/shared/plan-ready.flag
```

Print: `PLAN LISTO - [OPENCODE] codificando...`

---

## PHASE 2 - WAIT + MONITOR

Print: `[$CC_LABEL] Esperando a [$OC_LABEL]... (polling code-done.flag cada ~15s)`

Poll every ~15s. Individual Bash calls only - never a blocking loop:
```bash
ls {{AGENT_COLLAB_DIR}}/shared/code-done.flag {{AGENT_COLLAB_DIR}}/shared/error.flag 2>/dev/null; cat {{AGENT_COLLAB_DIR}}/shared/channel/planner_inbox.md 2>/dev/null
```

- `code-done.flag` -> Print: `[$OC_LABEL] Implementacion completa. Pasando a tests...` -> proceed to Phase 3
- `error.flag` -> Print: `[$OC_LABEL] ERROR detectado. Ver error.flag.` -> report to user and stop
- Inbox has content -> Print: `[$OC_LABEL -> $CC_LABEL] Mensaje recibido en inbox. Procesando...` -> process it, log response to `chat.log`, delegate to `opencode_inbox.md` if needed, clear inbox

Stay responsive to user questions during this phase - answer, then continue polling.

---

## PHASE 3 - TEST (Claude runs tests directly)

Print: `[$CC_LABEL] Ejecutando tests directamente con Bash...`

Run every test command from `plan.md` using the Bash tool. For each test:
- Print: `[$CC_LABEL] TEST: <command>`
- Run it with Bash
- Print `PASS +` or `FAIL X - <actual output>`

Do NOT delegate to OpenCode. Do NOT launch tmux sessions. Claude runs all tests inline.

**Use the Write tool** to write `{{AGENT_COLLAB_DIR}}/docs/results.md` with the full test report.
Print: `[$CC_LABEL] Escribiendo results.md...`

```bash
echo "$(date '+%H:%M:%S') [$CC_LABEL] Tests complete" >> {{AGENT_COLLAB_DIR}}/shared/run.log
```

**Token Usage Summary** - Claude runs directly via Bash:

```bash
{{AGENT_COLLAB_DIR}}/token-summary.sh
```

Then capture markdown version and append to results.md, and extract the run total to print explicitly:
```bash
SUMMARY_MD=$({{AGENT_COLLAB_DIR}}/token-summary.sh --markdown)
echo "" >> {{AGENT_COLLAB_DIR}}/docs/results.md
echo "$SUMMARY_MD" >> {{AGENT_COLLAB_DIR}}/docs/results.md

OC_SAVED=$({{AGENT_COLLAB_DIR}}/token-summary.sh | grep "Total:" | head -1 | awk '{print $NF}')
```

Print: `[$CC_LABEL] Tokens saved via OpenCode this run: $OC_SAVED (not charged to this Claude Code session)`

Print final verdict: `[$CC_LABEL] ALL TESTS PASSED` or `[$CC_LABEL] X TESTS FAILED - ver docs/results.md`

